### 4.4 REQ-LENS-009-004: Schema Compliance Verification

**Status**: To Be Implemented
**Priority**: High

**Rationale**: Verifying schema compliance prevents data quality issues and consumer failures

**Configuration**:
- Schema compatibility checking (backward, forward, full)
- Required field validation per schema
- Field type verification against schema definition
- Schema version tracking and alerting on changes
- Non-compliant message reporting with details

**Implementation Details**:
```json
// Example schema compliance check
{
  "topic": "customer-events",
  "schema_registry": "AWS Glue",
  "checks": [
    {
      "check_type": "schema_exists",
      "description": "Verify message has valid schema reference"
    },
    {
      "check_type": "required_fields",
      "description": "All required fields present",
      "fields": ["customerId", "eventType", "timestamp"]
    },
    {
      "check_type": "field_types",
      "description": "Fields match schema types",
      "validations": {
        "customerId": "string",
        "timestamp": "long (epoch millis)",
        "amount": "double"
      }
    },
    {
      "check_type": "schema_version",
      "description": "Alert on schema version changes",
      "alert_on_new_version": true
    }
  ],
  "reporting": {
    "non_compliant_sample_size": 100,
    "compliance_rate_threshold": 0.99
  }
}
```

**Validation**:
- Schema validation completes within 5 seconds per 1000 messages
- Non-compliant messages identified with specific errors
- Compliance rate accurately calculated

